 {"id":"CF-224","title":"verify-node assumes the node's address is reachable from the control host — true on a LAN node, false on a bunker, so a green node reports itself unverified","status":"pending","priority":"P1","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-05 on cf-node (bunker-las-03): the node's own ladder reached NODE: PASS (every rung green, manifest written, gateway answering /api/status 200 on 127.0.0.1:10800 and listening on 0.0.0.0:10800 inside the container), while scripts/verify-node.sh failed both its rows because it curls http://192.168.123.66:10800 from the control host and gets 000000: the container's LAN address is not routable from here. The result is a provisioner that reports INCOMPLETE (1) for a node that works, which trains an operator to ignore the last row.","acceptance_criteria":"1. specs/NODE.md defines the transport verify-node uses for a remote node, and why: a published port on the bunker host, a tunnel, or execution through the bunker CLI.\n2. verify-node implements that transport and says which one it used in its rows, with the measured code.\n3. A passing verify proves the gateway answers a request that did not originate inside the node — a loopback check inside the node is a FAIL, not a PASS, because it proves nothing about reachability.\n4. When the transport is unavailable, the row names it ('no published port for cf-node:10800') instead of printing 000000.\n5. docs/OPERATIONS.md and specs/NODE.md state plainly that a bunker node has no LAN address by default.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T03:08:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-05T03:08:09Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"de5bfdfd38e1c533991d0b9eb472e44955c3f165195bca7f50d59931a09155da"},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null}
 {"id":"CF-225","title":"claude-code: installer + variable contract + conformance legs, so a claude-* model can actually run on its native harness","status":"complete","priority":"P0","complexity":3,"reasoning":"specs/HARNESS-MATRIX.md §2 makes claude-* -> claude-code a rule, but nothing implements it end to end: crier has no claude adapter at all (audit 2026-11-05: grep claude over the Go tree hits only examples/agent-ecosystem/claude-code/Dockerfile:7) and scripts/harness/install-claude-code.sh is check-only, refusing on both branches. The adapter decision is CRIER-HARNESS-11; this row is the code-factory half.","acceptance_criteria":"1. install-claude-code.sh --apply installs a PINNED claude-code under $HOME, reads the version back, and is idempotent.\n2. It accepts the full CF_* set from specs/HARNESS-MATRIX.md §4 and REFUSES a credential passed as a value in argv (a negative test proves the refusal).\n3. One real turn on a node produces a known artifact and reports model_requested vs model_served.\n4. Rows in tests/harness-conformance.sh reach PASS/PASS/PASS/PASS for claude-code on a node with credentials, and SKIP naming the missing credential otherwise.\n5. The matrix in docs/HARNESS-CONFORMANCE.md is regenerated with claude-code's measured state.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-05T03:14:21Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T10:33:40Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"09a04c64fdafa0cea3d0315dc6539a8a69dd75ec9f69b2813caca429258d1355","evidence":[{"run_id":"2d2bac34","ts":"2026-11-06T10:33:40Z"}]},"capability_tags":[],"commit_hash":"7686bc81523e1da8c2d0bb951d2f64eef59d65c2","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":null,"foreman_note":"CF-225 advanced the conformance legs: leg_smoke resolves the harness binary from the adapter's own measured path (claude-code smoke no longer SKIPs on 'absent from PATH'; it now names the missing credential), with three selftest fixture arms including a red-proof of the pre-fix PATH-only leg. Implementation commits 2f07051 (b