 {"id": "CF-229", "title": "The CF_* variable contract: every harness installer and every harness invocation takes the same declared inputs \u2014 and refuses a credential in argv", "status": "complete", "priority": "P0", "complexity": 3, "reasoning": "specs/HARNESS-MATRIX.md \u00a74 fixes the set (CF_MODEL, CF_PROVIDER, CF_BASE_URL, CF_API_KEY_FILE, CF_WORKDIR, CF_NAMESPACE, CF_RUN_ID, CF_LANE, CF_SKILLS_DIR, CF_MAX_TURNS, CF_TIMEOUT_S). Today no installer accepts any of them: the adapters take --check/--apply and a few pin overrides, and the harness is invoked with a workdir and a text directive. The owner's requirement is that harnesses be 'able to pass in the variables to them'.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. Every scripts/harness/install-*.sh accepts the \u00a74 set (flags and CF_* env), documents it in --help, and ignores none of it silently.\n2. A credential supplied as a value in argv is REFUSED with a named failure; only a path is accepted (AGENTS.md r8), proven by a negative test per installer.\n3. An ambient provider key in the node's environment is not read: a test runs a harness with a bogus ambient key and asserts the run either fails or uses only the file.\n4. node-bus-worker.py passes the set from the directive to the harness, and records which values it passed.\n5. The conformance battery's vars leg is green for every harness in the matrix, and red when a variable is dropped.", "probe": null, "created_at": "2026-11-05T03:14:40Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-06T11:55:03Z", "detail": {"fingerprint": "ad5a44d13ad22e15710a886d8a3051084ce28042c4f2424de6f866d0884d1167", "evidence": [{"run_id":"d6fc04a4","ts":"2026-11-06T11:55:03Z","tree_fp":"70c394dd52e6faac0a6a007ba2c50a70fb9dd13fb506cec778e83710a262d309","artifacts":[".gitreins/history/2026-11-06/d6fc04a4/verdict.json"]}]}, "capability_tags": [], "commit_hash": "417449d", "guard_result": "SKIP", "ci_result": "SKIP", "worker_summary": "Verification close. No new contract code this tick: the contract landed in 4