-229-V1 judged this commit.", "foreman_note": "MEASURED 2026-11-06T00:49Z \u2014 implementation landed, row NOT complete, and the reason is a scope defect in my own acceptance criteria, stated plainly.\n\nLANDED: commit 45bd4bd on origin/main (proven ancestor of origin/main; sibling board-only commits 47a2ab0/769e061/a57d0db/38c1deb/2e0ec0c landed on top of it). scripts/harness/harness-vars.sh (new, 318 lines) is now the single implementation of \u00a75: all twelve declared names accepted as a flag AND as a CF_* environment variable; a credential VALUE in CF_API_KEY_FILE or via --api-key refused BY NAME (exit 2, length printed, value never echoed); CF_API_KEY set at all plus OPENAI_API_KEY/ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the ambient environment refused; CF_WORKDIR must resolve inside $HOME; budgets integer and ranged; CF_HARNESS_OPTS a key=value bag with no credential-shaped content \u2014 and every name recorded, so nothing is accepted and then silently ignored. install-hermes.sh gains --help, full acceptance and --contract (its CF-071 fixture anchors in tests/selftest.sh preserved). install-opencode.sh same, with --apply still refused as unmeasured. install-codex.sh aligned (CF_HARNESS_OPTS added, wrong \u00a74 citations corrected to \u00a75, a credential VALUE now refused by name instead of echoed back as a path). node-bus-worker.py exports only the directive's `vars`, scrubs every ambient CF_*, and records name+set+length in the result envelope; --check FAILs if any CF_* is set in the worker's own environment. tests/harness-conformance.sh gains a `vars` leg plus --vars-only that parses the declared set out of the spec rather than copying it.\n\nARMS I RAN MYSELF (not the worker's report): bash -n on all eight touched shell files rc=0; python3 -m py_compile scripts/node-bus-worker.py rc=0; tests/harness/vars-contract-test.sh rc=0 with 22 PASS / 0 FAIL; tests/harness-conformance.sh --vars-only => 6 pass, 2 fail, 0 skip; tests/selftest.sh => SELFTEST: PASS, EXIT=0, against a base that was also PASS before dispatch (so no inherited red was being absorbed). Mutation arm: appending a 13th declared row to \u00a75 turned the leg red BY NAME (\"\u00a75 declares CF_MUTATION_PROBE and this battery drops it \u2014 the set this battery checks is not the set \u00a75 declares\") and the spec was then restored byte-identically (sha256 cbc848d5ebebe41eccb6543059878f2df05e1b972735c0074861933f2cc0db51 before and after, git status clean). The leg is not decoration.\n\nTHE TWO FAILS ARE THE WHOLE STORY AND THEY ARE NOT THIS ROW'S TO FIX: deepseek:vars and pi-agent:vars fail with \"no adapter at scripts/harness/install-deepseek.sh\" / \"install-pi-agent.sh\". Neither harness has an installer at all \u2014 both were already FAIL on check/apply/smoke in the matrix before this change \u2014 so criterion 5 (\"green for every harness in the matrix\") is unsatisfiable from inside scripts/harness/*.sh: it requires CREATING two adapters, which is a different deliverable. Filed as CF-372; this row is blocked on it.\n\nGITREINS: task CF-229 completed at 2026-11-06T00:26:37Z; verdict run c8018623, judged commit 2e0ec0c (HEAD at judge time, which contains 45bd4bd), passed=false, INCOMPLETE \u2014 \"evaluation hit resource cap before all criteria verified\", with partial evidence that agrees with my own numbers (vars-contract 22/0/1 PASS; --vars-only 6/2; node-bus-worker wiring at lines 89-100, 487-558, 1044; and docs/HARNESS-CONFORMANCE.md has no vars column). I am NOT closing on that verdict, and I am NOT editing criterion 5 down to fit the code: the criterion is right, the tree is short of it, and CF-372 is the missing piece. Re-judge after CF-372 lands.\n\nA RESIDUAL THE VERDICT IS RIGHT ABOUT EITHER WAY: docs/HARNESS-CONFORMANCE.md carries no vars column, because --write-doc runs the smoke legs and needs live harness credentials this row does not have. Do not hand-edit it; regenerate it after CF-372.\n\nCI: none configured \u2014 .github/workflows absent and `gh 